		{
			"id": "eg_Np9ykrjq4FZgSD",
			"description": "Gauss Blaster",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The standard-issue weapon of the Necron Immortals: a heavier-cased gauss weapon that Codex: Necrons and Black Library's Necron fiction both single out as a genuine threat to Astartes- grade armour where the rank-and-file Warrior's flayer is not, matching the Immortals' consistent depiction as the tougher, more dangerous line troops standing behind a Warrior phalanx.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's own anchor: \"Gauss blaster | 7d(3) burn, RoF 3.\" Kept at the same divisor (4) the Gauss Flayer above is built to (the anchor calls both weapons \"gauss,\" the same underlying disassembly-beam physics, so the divisor should not differ weapon to weapon within the family) but one die heavier, matching the anchor's own die increase over the flayer. Checked by exact dice distribution: 7d(4) burn averages 24.5 and penetrates flak (DR 30, eff. 7.5) 100% of the time, carapace (DR 70, eff. 17.5) 93.9%, Astartes power armour (DR 100, eff. 25) 41.4% - a real, regular threat to a Space Marine, not merely \"occasionally\" - and a Terminator (DR 200, eff. 50) 0%, exactly matching the fiction's \"Immortals can actually hurt a Marine; a flayer mostly can't.\" Handling: 20 lb, heavier again than the flayer for the Immortal's reinforced dual-barrel housing; min ST 15† (sqrt(10x20)=14.1, bumped for the same dense, ungiving Necron grip as the flayer) sits comfortably under an Immortal's own ST 28. RoF 3, Bulk -5 and Rcl 1 are unchanged from the flayer's own derivation - same mechanism, same handling class, just a bigger beam. Acc 6 is likewise unchanged. Shots 250(3600), slightly fewer pulses than the flayer's 300 before the same hour-long reactor recharge, for the bigger draw per shot.",
