		{
			"id": "eqyZkq-VN6o8Q78Jq",
			"description": "Gauss Cannon",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A heavy support gauss weapon carried by specialist Necron troops (and mounted on Tomb Blades and Canoptek constructs in larger form); Codex: Necrons background and the RPG-line Necron-armoury material describe it as the family's dedicated squad-support pattern, pouring far more disassembling energy into a single beam than a flayer or blaster while firing markedly slower.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's own anchor: \"Gauss cannon | 6d×2(3) burn.\" Kept at the literal anchor divisor (3), one step gentler than the flayer/blaster's re-read (4), since a cannon-class weapon's own doubled damage does the real work of moving it up the family rather than needing the smaller weapons' divisor correction. Checked by exact dice distribution: 6dx2(3) averages 42 and penetrates carapace (DR 70, eff. 23.3) 99.0%, Astartes power armour (DR 100, eff. 33.3) 85.5%, and even a Terminator (DR 200, eff. 66.7) 0.06% - a genuine Marine-killer, and the first weapon in the family with any measurable Terminator threat at all, matching its role as a dedicated support weapon rather than an infantry sidearm. Handling: 35 lb, a real two-Necron-portable support weapon; min ST 20B (raw sqrt(10x35)=18.7, rounded up and given the B suffix since every depiction shows it braced or crewed rather than shoulder-fired by one Warrior alone). RoF 1: the bigger single discharge needs a real recharge between shots, unlike the flayer/blaster's rapid pulses. Shots 60(120): a genuinely smaller reserve than the lighter weapons' reactor-fed figures, with a two-minute recharge, reflecting the much larger single draw per shot rather than a magazine limit. Bulk -7 and Acc 6 (unchanged beam-weapon allowance) fit a heavy support weapon; Rcl 1 is unchanged - still a coherent beam with no reaction mass.",
