		{
			"id": "e0X8TU4OdBxrLGdZp",
			"description": "Heavy Gauss Cannon",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The family's dedicated anti-armour pattern, mounted on Doomsday Arks, Tomb Blades and carried arm-integrated by Canoptek and Destroyer-class Necron constructs; Codex: Necrons background and Black Library's Necron fiction both treat it as capable of cracking open a battle tank or a Terminator's plate with a single well-placed beam, the gauss family's answer to a lascannon.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's own anchor: \"Heavy gauss cannon | Anti-armour: 6d×4(5) burn.\" Held at the anchor exactly, since it already delivers the promised result: checked by exact dice distribution, 6dx4(5) averages 84 and clears every personal-armour DR on the framework's table at 99.6%-100%, including a Terminator (DR 200, eff. 40) at 99.55%. At the current 6dx5(5) cor it clears the vehicle table at 79.4%-100% across AV10-14 (AV14, DR 440, eff. 88, still 79.4%) but never gets through a Leman Russ's front or a Land Raider (DR 1350, eff. 270) on one hit, where a lascannon gets 13%; each hit still eats DR from the plate, penetrating or not, so sustained fire wears even that down - a genuine anti-armour weapon, exactly matching \"can crack a tank or a Terminator\" without inflating it to guaranteed overkill everywhere. Handling: 60 lb, built into a Destroyer- or Canoptek-class chassis's own weapon arm rather than carried loose - the raw formula gives sqrt(10x60)=24.5, kept as a literal ST figure with the M suffix (mounted, here meaning integral to the wielding construct's own frame, the same convention this project's Kataphron Eradication Ray entry uses) rather than assuming a Warrior-scale wielder. RoF 1 and a small 20(300) reserve (a five-minute recharge) reflect the huge single discharge. Bulk -8 is nominal since the weapon is never unslung. Acc 5, one point below the lighter gauss weapons, since this pattern is built for raw punch at moderate range rather than fine target discrimination. Rcl 1 is unchanged.",
