		{
			"id": "evePa0kuRy9cDsXzZ",
			"description": "Tesla Carbine",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A lighter, crackling energy weapon fielded alongside gauss arms, most associated with Immortals, Tomb Blades and other Necron troops who favour a weapon that punishes a crowd rather than a single hard target; Codex: Necrons background and Black Library's Necron fiction both describe tesla weapons arcing wildly between nearby targets on contact, lighting up whole groups of enemy infantry in a single burst rather than punching cleanly through one target's armour.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's own anchor: \"Tesla carbine | 6d(2) burn with arcs that jump to nearby targets on a hit (like volkite chains).\" Held at the anchor's own divisor (2) and dice exactly, since the anchor is explicit and the weapon's real threat is the arc, not raw penetration: checked by exact dice distribution, 6d(2) averages 21 and penetrates flak (DR 30, eff. 15) 90.4% of the time but rounds to 0% against carapace (DR 70, eff. 35) or anything heavier - a real anti-infantry weapon and no threat at all to rigid plate on its own, exactly the gap the arc effect is built to cross by simply hitting more targets rather than hitting any one of them harder. Handling: 12 lb, the lightest weapon in this file, for a carbine-length housing sized for an Immortal's or Tomb Blade's own build; min ST 12† (sqrt(10x12)=11, bumped one for the same ungiving Necron grip as the gauss family) sits well under any Necron's ST. RoF 4 (faster than the gauss family's RoF 3, since firing quickly to maximise arc triggers is exactly what this weapon is built to do) and Shots 200(1800), a half-hour reactor recharge for a smaller reserve than the gauss flayer's. Bulk -4 (one step lighter than a full gauss rifle, matching its carbine build) and Rcl 1 (coherent discharge) round out the entry. Acc 5, one point below a full gauss rifle's, since a tesla weapon is built for volume over precision.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Necrons"
			],
			"tech_level": "12^",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "3600",
			"base_weight": "12 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "WUp-P5QFllfL7NcDA",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "burn",
						"base": "6d",
						"armor_divisor": 2
					},
					"accuracy": "5",
					"range": "120/360",
					"rate_of_fire": "4",
					"shots": "200(1800)",
					"bulk": "-4",
					"recoil": "1",
					"strength": "12†",
					"usage": "Standard",
					"usage_notes": "Arc effect (framework.md): any hit, not only a kill, releases a crackling secondary bolt at up to two other valid targets within 3 yards, each resolved as a single ordinary Beam Weapons attack roll at this weapon's own stats - the same \"reuse an ordinary attack roll rather than invent a new mechanic\" approach this project's Volkite entries use for their own chain-on-kill effect, adapted here to trigger on any hit at all (not only a kill) per tesla's own, more permissive lore description and per this weapon's lighter per-bolt damage, which would otherwise almost never trigger a kill-only chain against anything but an unarmoured target.",
					"defaults": [
