		{
			"id": "eEvUK6Jr2B05Likrw",
			"description": "Tesla Cannon",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A heavier tesla weapon mounted on Annihilation Barges and other heavy Necron constructs; background material treats it as the family's squad-support pattern, keeping the carbine's signature arcing but with enough raw punch behind each bolt to threaten real armour as well as saturate a firing line.\n\nDesign: No framework anchor names this pattern directly, so it is built one size class up from the Tesla Carbine anchor the same way the Gauss Cannon steps up from the Gauss Blaster: the carbine's own dice doubled (6dx2, keeping the family's (2) divisor since the underlying arc-discharge physics is unchanged) rather than simply adding more dice, matching the family's own established \"double the base weapon's dice for the support-class pattern\" relationship the gauss family uses. Checked by exact dice distribution: 6dx2(2) averages 42 and penetrates flak (DR 30, eff. 15) 99.98%, carapace (DR 70, eff. 35) 79.4%, Astartes power armour (DR 100, eff. 50) 14.5%, and rounds to 0% against a Terminator - a real, if occasional, threat to power armour on top of the carbine's own arc-and-saturate role, matching a heavier support weapon's place in the family. Handling: 24 lb and min ST 17B (sqrt(10x24)=15.5, bumped for the same dense grip convention, braced since every depiction shows it crewed or shoulder-braced rather than hand-carried at speed). RoF 3, matching the carbine's own \"fire fast to trigger arcs\" logic at a heavier weapon's scale; Shots 100(1800), half the carbine's reserve for the bigger per-shot draw at the same half-hour recharge. Bulk -6 and Acc 6 sit between the carbine and the gauss cannon; Rcl 1 is unchanged.",
