		{
			"id": "e_GpcsftYa2C49a0e",
			"description": "Synaptic Disintegrator",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Necron Deathmark's own sniper weapon: a rifle built for a single, unerring shot at an enemy officer, psyker or other priority target, fired from ambush after a Deathmark phases in from concealment. Codex: Necrons background and Black Library's Necron fiction (Deathmark squads feature in several Twice-Dead King and Infinite and the Divine passages) treat it as one of the most accurate weapons the Necron armoury fields, purpose-built to drop a single well-armoured priority target rather than to sustain fire.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's own anchor: \"Synaptic disintegrator | Sniper, 8d(3) burn, very high Acc.\" The divisor is bumped to (4), matching the same anchor-vs-prose correction the Gauss Flayer above makes, since a dedicated anti-elite sniper weapon that only occasionally drops the power-armoured target it exists to snipe would contradict its own role: checked by exact dice distribution, 8d(4) burn averages 28 and penetrates carapace (DR 70, eff. 17.5) 98.6% of the time and Astartes power armour (DR 100, eff. 25) 69.5% of the time - a real, reliable threat to exactly the armoured commanders and elite troops a Deathmark is sent to remove - while a Terminator (DR 200, eff. 50) still drops to 0%, keeping it well short of a dedicated anti-armour weapon. Handling: 18 lb, a long, precision-built rifle heavier than a plain gauss flayer for its focusing array; min ST 14† (sqrt(10x18)=13.4, bumped one for the dense Necron grip) sits comfortably under a Deathmark's own ST 26. RoF 1 (a single deliberate shot, never depicted fired rapidly) and Shots 40(1800), a modest reserve with a half-hour recharge, reflecting a weapon built for one perfect shot per ambush rather than sustained fire. Bulk -6 (long and precision-barrelled) and Rcl 1 (coherent beam) round out the entry. Acc 10: the anchor's own \"very high Acc\" read literally as matching the Imperium's dedicated heavy-sniper class (the Transuranic Arquebus sits at Acc 8; this project gives the Deathmark's own purpose- built sniper weapon two points over that, reflecting the same \"cannot miss what it targets\" role the fiction gives it).",
