		{
			"id": "es_AWLhRtydRzBf7Y",
			"description": "Particle Caster",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A compact particle-beam sidearm carried by Necron Overlords and Royal Wardens as a badge of rank alongside a warscythe or hyperphase sword; particle weapons appear across Codex: Necrons background and older Necron material (the tabletop's historical \"particle whip\"/\"particle projector\" family) as a distinct energy-weapon lineage from gauss and tesla, built around a contained, accelerated particle stream rather than an entropic beam or an electrical arc.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's anchor gives the family shape rather than fixed dice: \"Particle beamer / caster | Particle weapons: burn ex, scale from plasma.\" Built as a pistol-class particle weapon scaled the same distance below the rifle-class Particle Beamer below that this project's own Imperium Plasma Pistol sits below the Plasma Gun (two dice down, divisor unchanged): 4dx3(3) burn ex. Checked by exact dice distribution: average 42 damage penetrates carapace (DR 70, eff. 23.3) 97.3%, Astartes power armour (DR 100, eff. 33.3) 76.1%, and even a Terminator (DR 200, eff. 66.7) 0.4% - a genuinely dangerous sidearm befitting an Overlord's own personal weapon, well above what a plasma pistol manages against the same targets, matching a Necron noble's superior archeotech over Imperial reverse-engineering. Handling: 8 lb, a heavy relic sidearm rather than a light Imperial-style pistol, per the framework's \"Necron weapons are heavy\" instruction even at pistol scale; min ST 10† (sqrt(10x8)=8.9, bumped one for the same dense grip convention as the rest of this file) sits well under an Overlord's own ST 34. RoF 1 and Shots 20(1800) (a half-hour recharge) reflect a genuine capacitor-class discharge that must build again between shots, the same \"must recharge\" bracket framework.md gives plasma weapons. Bulk -3 and Rcl 1 fit a heavy but still one-handed sidearm. Acc 4, the pistol bracket's high end plus a partial beam- weapon allowance, since this is a rank-and-file badge weapon rather than a dedicated long-range tool.",
