		{
			"id": "ekE7H-7kge9RQXYjs",
			"description": "Particle Beamer",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A rifle-scale particle weapon carried by senior Necron nobles and Crypteks who want a genuine anti-Astartes tool rather than a badge sidearm; older Necron background and the RPG-line Necron-armoury material both place particle weapons alongside gauss and tesla as the third pillar of Necron small-arms technology, distinct in feel (a contained, focused beam rather than a dissolving ray or a crackling arc) even where their end result on a target is comparably lethal.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's own instruction, read directly: \"scale from plasma.\" Held exactly at the Imperium Plasma Gun's own anchor dice (6dx4(3) burn ex) rather than a re-derived figure, since the anchor gives no reason to move it and the underlying physics (a contained, accelerated energy bolt) is close enough to plasma that matching it directly is the honest choice - the same judgement this project's Aeldari Starcannon entry makes against the same anchor. Checked by exact dice distribution: average 84 damage penetrates Astartes power armour (DR 100, eff. 33.3) 99.9% of the time and a Terminator (DR 200, eff. 66.7) 85.5% of the time, identical to the Imperium Plasma Gun's own verified figures - a genuine top-tier anti-Astartes weapon, matching Necron particle technology's reputation as at least the Imperium's own plasma family's equal. Handling: 20 lb, a real two-handed rifle-class weapon heavier than the particle caster for its full accelerator housing; min ST 15† (sqrt(10x20)=14.1, bumped one for the dense Necron grip) sits well under a noble Necron's own ST. RoF 1 and Shots 20(1800) (the same half-hour recharge as the caster, for a bigger single reserve of accumulated charge) match the anchor's own \"must recharge\" plasma-class mechanism, and unlike the Imperium plasma family this weapon has no supercharge/Malf line at all - a Necron particle weapon's containment is a matter of the wielder's own ancient reactor, not a fallible coil prone to overheating, so there is nothing here for a malfunction roll to represent. Bulk -6 and Acc 6 fit a rifle-class weapon; Rcl 1 is unchanged.",
