		{
			"id": "exteAH3Kj_PL79-f8",
			"description": "Particle Whip",
			"local_notes": "Lore: In its usual form the particle whip is the main weapon of the Monolith, lashing a heavy particle beam back and forth across an enemy line; this personal-scale entry covers the rarer variant Codex: Necrons and older background material occasionally describe mounted on an individual heavy Necron construct or carried as a staff-weapon by a senior Cryptek or Technomancer overseeing a Tomb World's awakening, rather than the vehicle-scale turret every other depiction shows.\n\nDesign: Built one die and one multiplier step above the Particle Beamer above, the same \"heaviest personal-scale pattern in the family\" relationship this project's Tesla Destructor and Enmitic Annihilator entries below use for their own families: 7dx4(3) burn ex. Checked by exact dice distribution: average 98 damage clears every personal-armour DR at 96.2%+ (including a Terminator, DR 200, eff. 66.7, at 96.2%) and the vehicle table at 80.8%-100% across AV10-12, dropping to 19.2% at AV13 and 0.3% at AV14 (DR 440, eff. 146), and 0% against a Leman Russ's front or a Land Raider (DR 1350) - a genuinely fearsome weapon at personal scale without matching the true vehicle-mounted turret's own effectively unlimited damage output, appropriate for a hand- or staff-carried variant rather than a Monolith's main weapon. Handling: 40 lb and min ST 21M (sqrt(10x40)=20, bumped one and given the M suffix since every depiction of a personal-scale particle whip shows it integrated into a heavy construct's own chassis or a Cryptek's staff-mount rather than freely carried); RoF 1 and a small 10(3600) reserve (a full hour's recharge) reflect the largest single discharge in the particle family. Bulk -8 and Rcl 1 fit a genuinely heavy weapon; Acc 6 is unchanged from the lighter particle weapons.",
