		{
			"id": "eKptG53JR7ILE4Wf0",
			"description": "Gauss Reaper",
			"local_notes": "Lore: HOUSE VARIANT, not a Codex weapon: a heavy, rapid-firing chassis-mounted gauss cannon for a Destroyer-cult or other heavy Necron construct (the Codex's own \"gauss reaper\" is a short- range Warrior-pattern weapon, and Skorpekh Destroyers carry only their reap-blade and threshing weapons, so this is not fielded on the Skorpekh template). Use the Enmitic Exterminator or Annihilator below for the canonical ranged Destroyers.\n\nDesign: Built between the Gauss Cannon and Heavy Gauss Cannon anchors, as a house weapon heavier- hitting than a standard support trooper but not a dedicated anti-tank platform: the Gauss Cannon's own dice (6dx2) pushed one multiplier step further (6dx3) at the shared family divisor (3). Checked by exact dice distribution: average 63 damage penetrates Astartes power armour (DR 100, eff. 33.3) 99.0% of the time and a Terminator (DR 200, eff. 66.7) 36.3% of the time - a serious, reliable threat to power armour and a real (if unlikely to be decisive alone) threat to the heaviest personal armour in the game, exactly the gap between \"support trooper's gun\" and \"dedicated anti-tank cannon\" a Destroyer-cult weapon-arm should occupy. Handling: 50 lb, built directly into a construct's weapon-arm rather than carried, so the raw formula (sqrt(10x50)=22.4) is kept as a literal ST figure with the M suffix, the same convention this project's Kataphron Eradication Ray and this file's own Heavy Gauss Cannon use for chassis-integrated weapons. RoF 3 (a rapid-firing cannon suited to a fast- moving construct, matching the flayer/blaster family's own RoF rather than the slower support-class cannons) and Shots 150(3600), a full hour's recharge for a large but not maximal reserve. Bulk -7 is nominal (never unslung) and Rcl 1 is unchanged; Acc 6 matches the rest of the gauss family.",
