		{
			"id": "eUqe-14ODEVj8ciy4",
			"description": "Enmitic Exterminator",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The gun-arm weapon of the flying Necron Destroyer cult: standard Destroyers carry the gauss-pattern Enmitic Exterminator, an anti-infantry weapon built into their hover-chassis arm, while the larger, slower Heavy Destroyer variant swaps it for the far more powerful particle-pattern Enmitic Annihilator, a dedicated tank-and-Terminator killer. Codex: Necrons background and Black Library's Necron fiction consistently draw the two apart exactly this way: the same cult and the same chassis family, two different weapon-arms for two different jobs, so this project keeps them as one entry's two usage lines rather than two unrelated weapons.\n\nDesign: The Exterminator line is built as a rifle-to-cannon-scale gauss weapon between the Gauss Blaster and Gauss Cannon anchors, at the family's own established (3) divisor: 7dx2(3) burn, checked by exact dice distribution to average 49 damage and penetrate Astartes power armour (DR 100, eff. 33.3) 96.2% of the time, a Terminator (DR 200, eff. 66.7) 2.2% of the time - a reliable Marine-killer with only a token threat to the heaviest personal armour, matching \"anti-infantry\" precisely. The Annihilator line instead scales from the particle family the same way the Enmitic name-pair itself implies a shared chassis with two different internals: 6dx4(4) burn ex, one divisor step better than the Particle Beamer's (3) for a dedicated, single-purpose anti-armour mount rather than a general-purpose rifle. Checked by exact dice distribution: average 84 clears every personal-armour DR at 98.0%+ (Terminator, DR 200, eff. 50, at 98.0%) and the vehicle table at 90.4%-100% across AV10-12, 45.4% at AV13 and 6.1% at AV14 (DR 440, eff. 110), with 0% against a Leman Russ's front or a Land Raider (DR 1350) - a real killer of light and medium vehicles, distinctly ahead of the standard Exterminator and matching the Heavy Destroyer's own place in the fiction as the cult's dedicated anti-armour specialist. Handling: both lines are built into their respective chassis's own weapon-arm, so both use the M suffix with the raw ST formula kept literal rather than adjusted for a carried grip: Exterminator at 45 lb (sqrt(10x45)=21.2) and Annihilator at a heavier 70 lb for its bigger accelerator core (sqrt(10x70)=26.5). RoF 3 for the Exterminator (a fast anti-infantry gauss cannon, matching the Gauss Reaper's own rate) against RoF 1 for the Annihilator (a single heavy particle discharge that must fully recharge, matching the particle family's own mechanism); Shots and recharge times scale the same way, a bigger reserve for the lighter, faster-cycling Exterminator. Bulk is nominal for both (never unslung) and Rcl 1 is unchanged; Acc 6 for the Exterminator matches the gauss family, Acc 5 for the Annihilator matches the Heavy Gauss Cannon's own slightly lower figure for a weapon built for punch over precision.",
