		{
			"id": "eA1cnHQbpotqp_2HW",
			"description": "Tachyon Arrow",
			"local_notes": "Lore: An archeotech relic weapon of the Triarch, referenced in Codex: Necrons background and Black Library's Necron fiction as one of the single most devastating personal weapons in the Necron arsenal precisely because it is fired so rarely - a single, near-unstoppable shot that has been described killing targets other anti-armour weapons could not touch, at the cost of an enormous recharge before it can be fired again.\n\nDesign: No framework anchor names this weapon by dice, only by role (\"one-shot anti-everything relic\"), so it is built as this project's top-tier personal energy weapon, the same \"hero weapon\" precedent the Imperium Solar Atomiser and Aeldari Wraithcannon entries establish: checked by exact dice distribution, 6dx6(10) burn averages 126 and clears every DR on both the personal-armour and AV10-14 vehicle tables at 100%, including a Terminator (DR 200, eff. 20) and AV14 (DR 440, eff. 44), but gets through a Leman Russ's front or a Land Raider's glacis (DR 1350, eff. 135) only 36.3% of the time - \"anti-everything\" short of the very heaviest tank armour, where it still beats a lascannon's 13%, appropriate for a weapon the fiction only ever shows fired once per engagement, if that. Handling: 10 lb, an oddly light, elegant device for what it does, per its archeotech origin outside even standard Necron manufacture; min ST 11† (sqrt(10x10)=10, bumped for an unfamiliar grip) is a trivial figure for any Necron noble who might carry it. RoF 1 and the 1(3600*) shot line above are the weapon's whole design point rather than an afterthought. Bulk -4 and Rcl 1 fit a rifle-class relic; Acc 8, well above any other weapon in this file, reflects a weapon the fiction shows always finding its mark. LC0 as the rest of this file, and a six-figure notional cost mark it as unique, GM-reference equipment rather than anything a standard Necron formation is issued.",
