					"strength": "11†",
					"usage": "Standard (single use)",
					"usage_notes": "A relic of the Triarch's own arsenal: firing it collapses the projectile through a sliver of folded spacetime so it strikes its target before it can be dodged, aimed or intercepted by any conventional defence (GM's discretion whether an active regenerating shield or void shield still absorbs the hit as SP - the arrow is unerring, not immaterial). The 1(3600*) shot count means exactly that: after firing, the weapon is spent until its housing is returned to a working Tomb World's own power network to rebuild the charge, a process the fiction never shows taking less than a full scene and which the GM should usually treat as \"not available again this session\" rather than a literal one-hour countdown.",
