		{
			"id": "e1uaR6JTO6YsUXx2B",
			"description": "Staff of Light",
			"local_notes": "Melee field-on line carries armour divisor (10), per the framework's power-field rule; with the field off it is a plain staff (sw cr). This is one physical weapon with both a ranged and a melee mode; it is included wholesale into the Ranged Weapons file per data-format.md's `include` convention (the same pattern the Aeldari Singing Spear uses across melee.yaml and ranged.yaml) rather than defined twice.\n\nLore: A dual-purpose energy staff carried by Necron Lords, Overlords and Crypteks as both a badge of authority and a working weapon: Codex: Necrons background and older Necron material both describe it firing a bolt of disintegrating energy at range, then serving as a power-field melee weapon when its wielder is forced into close combat - a generalist's tool rather than either family's dedicated specialist.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's own anchor: \"Staff of light | Energy staff: ranged 6d(3) burn and a power- field melee strike.\" The ranged line is held at the anchor's literal dice and divisor (3) rather than the Gauss Flayer's bumped (4), since this is deliberately a generalist's badge weapon rather than a front-line infantry rifle - checked by exact dice distribution, 6d(3) burn averages 21 and penetrates flak (DR 30, eff. 10) 99.6% of the time but only 27.9% against carapace (DR 70, eff. 23.3) and 0.06% against Astartes power armour, a real anti- infantry weapon and a poor anti-Astartes one, exactly what a Lord's sidearm should be next to a dedicated Warrior or Immortal weapon. The melee line applies this project's own power- field rule (divisor (10) written into the damage string, with a field-off line at the plain staff's sw cr) but with a smaller field step (+2d rather than the usual +3d), one die lighter than the Hyperphase Sword's own sw+3d, since a staff's melee mode is a secondary function of a primarily ranged item rather than a dedicated blade: checked by exact dice distribution at ST 10 (sw=1d, giving 3d(10)): average 10.5 damage penetrates flak/carapace/Sororitas at 100%/99.6%/98.8% and Astartes power armour (DR 100, eff. 10) 94.6% of the time, and a Terminator (DR 200, eff. 20) 9.7% - genuinely dangerous in a pinch, well below the Hyperphase Sword's own figures at the higher ST a dedicated melee wielder would bring, an honest consequence of a Lord's own more modest ST when caught fighting with a badge weapon rather than a proper blade in hand. Handling: 10 lb and min ST 10 for a staff meant to be genuinely comfortable in a Necron Lord's hand rather than built heavy like a rank-and-file trooper's weapon - the one item in this file with no \"no ergonomic concession\" bump, since a Lord's own staff is exactly the item a Necron would bother to make comfortable. RoF 2 and Shots 100(1800) (a half-hour recharge) sit between the Tesla Carbine's rapid pulses and the Gauss Cannon's slow single shots, matching a generalist weapon's middling cycle rate. Bulk -4 and Rcl 1 are unchanged from the rest of this armoury; Acc 5 sits at the low end of the rifle bracket for a weapon not built primarily as a marksman's tool. Reach 1 and parry 0 (Staff's own Basic Set convention) fit the melee mode.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Necrons"
			],
